\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf2\ulc0\insrsid1319977\charrsid13444761 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13444761 {\b\f38\fs22\cf2\ulc0\insrsid13444761\charrsid13444761 Body Language: }{\f39\fs22\cf2\ulc0\insrsid13444761\charrsid13444761 
Stand rather than sit when you are delivering your presentation and try to be
\par aware of any repetitive hand gestures or awkward mannerisms that might irritate your audience.
\par }{\b\f38\fs22\cf2\ulc0\insrsid13444761\charrsid13444761 Voice Quality: }{\f39\fs22\cf2\ulc0\insrsid13444761\charrsid13444761 You must be clearly audible at all times \endash  don\rquote t let your voice drop at the end of
\par sentences. If you vary your intonation, your voice will be more interesting to listen to and you will be able to
\par make your points more effectively.
\par }{\b\f38\fs22\cf2\ulc0\insrsid13444761\charrsid13444761 Visual aids: }{\f39\fs22\cf2\ulc0\insrsid13444761\charrsid13444761 You your visual aids confidently, making sure you allow your audience time to absorb
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13444761 {\f39\fs22\cf2\ulc0\insrsid13444761\charrsid13444761 information from flipcharts and transparencies.}{\cf2\ulc0\insrsid13444761\charrsid13444761 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf0\ulc0\insrsid1319977     }{\b\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid1319977 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\cf0\ulc0\insrsid1319977 Question No: 25    ( Marks: 3 ) 
